From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Tue, 8 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: fold the players of the first half of libduel for n > 2

Every Lua function of libduel.cpp from the top to GetChainEvent that takes
or returns a player now uses the fold API of fold.h. Only libduel.cpp
changes.

Individual actions (the player acts or is acted on) go through
unfold_action: SetLP, Recover, PayLPCost, Win, Draw, Equip, GetControl,
ChangeBattleDamage, ChangeTargetPlayer, DiscardDeck, DiscardHand, the three
Shuffle functions, the sort and confirm-top functions, Summon, MSet, SSet,
CreateToken, SpecialSummon (both players), the summon-rule functions,
RegisterEffect, the flag effect setters, RemoveCounter, MoveToField (both
players, so the place prompt goes to the chooser), and the reason and target
players of Destroy, Remove, Sendto*, Release.

Individual queries use query_list and give the best case over the living
opponents: GetTurnCount, GetDrawCount, GetFlagEffect, GetFlagEffectLabel,
IsCanAddCounter, GetChainMaterial, CheckLPCost, GetBattleDamage, the zone
count functions, the linked group, count and zone functions, GetFieldCard,
CheckLocation. Field functions use field_side or field_list:
IsCanRemoveCounter, GetCounter (the counter flags swap) and ConfirmCards
(one message for every duelist of the other side). IsEnvironment compares
the folded side. The player results of CheckEvent, GetEnvironment,
GetChainInfo and GetChainEvent use push_player. RaiseEvent and
RaiseSingleEvent unfold their event players.

Five static helpers at the top of the file, all named f3a_: optional player
arguments keep their core default when the script gives none, an invalid
value never reaches a prompt or an index, and the player slot is pinned
before a yield that reads it again.

With 2 duelists nothing changes. No scope folds and every helper is the
identity. The n=2 message bytes stay the same.

